  "semantics": [
    "A run standard admits exactly the tools it lists, matched as exact strings; a listed tool's call that names an amount (amount_minor or amount) must carry an integer amount_minor in the standard's currency, spelled exactly, at most the limit (inclusive); a call naming no amount passes on the list alone.",
    "A payment standard (a limit, no run block) admits only the one tool its enforcement block names, and every call to it must carry an integer amount_minor in the standard's currency within the limit.",
    "A standard that states neither tools nor a limit admits nothing at the gate.",
    "A call the gate admits whose amount is above the named person's threshold is held for that person, never refused and never passed."
  ],
  "decisions": {
    "allow": "the gate signs an allow receipt",
    "deny": "the gate refuses before the call runs",
    "hold": "the gate holds the call for the named person on the standard's page"
  },
